-                            image, tag),
+                        msg="The requested image does not exist: {}".format(
+                            self.image_reference()),
                         failed=True
                     )
                 else:
diff --git a/releasenotes/notes/kolla-container-image-digests-410e068985c1ba8d.yaml b/releasenotes/notes/kolla-container-image-digests-410e068985c1ba8d.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..4ff3ec245
--- /dev/null
+++ b/releasenotes/notes/kolla-container-image-digests-410e068985c1ba8d.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+---
+fixes:
+  - |
+    The ``kolla_container`` module now accepts an image given by digest,
+    such as ``quay.io/openstack.kolla/keystone@sha256:<hex>``, for example
+    in a ``<service>_image_full`` variable. With Docker, pulling such an
+    image failed, because the digest was sent to the Docker API as a tag
+    named after its hexadecimal part. Docker's classic image store also
+    lists an image pulled by digest without a tag, so a container using one
+    was found to differ from its image, and was recreated, on every run.
+    Podman already pulled images by digest. Changing a container's image
+    from a tag to a digest recreates the container once, as any change to
+    its image does.
